The attached image conceptually illustrates the dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle, Nano-11, derived from phytoglycogen. Each spherical representation is cut away to reveal a dense, highly branched internal structure originating from a central core, characteristic of dendrimers. The outer layer represents the chemically modified surface of the nanoparticle, which in Nano-11 carries a positive charge. This modification enables the electrostatic adsorption of negatively charged protein antigens, as described in the accompanying text, facilitating its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.